# CLI reference

The workspace provides `rocci` for template modules and runtime applications, `rocdown` for Markdown documents and static sites, and `rocci-okf` for knowledge bundle review and retrieval.

Examples below use `cargo run` from a source checkout. Installed binaries use
the same arguments without the Cargo prefix.

## Rocci CLI

### Validate configuration

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- validate [rocci.toml]
```

Parse and validate the application configuration. Unknown fields and unsafe
runtime settings are errors.

### Build .rocci template to Roc

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- build INPUT [-o OUTPUT]
```

Compile a single `.rocci` template to Roc. With `-o`, write to the given path;
otherwise print to stdout.

### Inspect template source and AST

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- inspect INPUT [--ast] [--segments]
```

Inspect compiled information: component signatures, fixtures, styles, handlers,
and source map segments. `--ast` prints the parsed AST as an S-expression.

### Run a single component

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- view INPUT [--component NAME] [--arg name=val] [--port PORT] [--no-window]
```

Run a component with mock arguments and an optional state type. The component
is wrapped in a minimal application and launched in a native window.

### Browse components

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- browse [DIRECTORY] [--port PORT] [--no-window]
```

Discover and interactively browse all `.rocci` components and fixtures in a directory.

### Run an application

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- run [ENTRY] [--port PORT] [--no-window] [--args...]
```

Run the entry template or directory. The application server starts and opens a
preview window by default. The preview overlay supports current-document find
(`Cmd/Ctrl-F`, `E` for selection, `G` / `Shift-G` to move, wrapping at the
ends) and go-to-file (`Cmd/Ctrl-K`). Static site and knowledge review servers
expose a Dev control that opens a profiling panel; `rocci run` serves that
panel on a sibling loopback port so it is not injected into the authored app's
routes. `--no-window` prints timings on stderr instead.

| Option | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `--no-window` | Serve without opening the preview window |
| `--port PORT` | Override the listening port (defaults to a free port, or 8000 with `--no-window`) |
| `--args...` | Extra arguments forwarded to the Roc binary |

### Bundle a macOS app

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- bundle [--config rocci.toml]
```

Build a local ad-hoc-signed macOS app bundle. Other packaging targets are not
implemented yet.

### Datastar asset management

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- datastar pin [VERSION] [--app PATH]
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- datastar update [--app PATH]
```

Pin or update the Datastar JavaScript runtime asset in an application directory.

---

## Rocdown CLI

### Run an interactive document or documentation site

```sh
# Run a single interactive document
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- run report.rocdown

# Run a documentation site directory with live reload
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- run [ROOT] [--port PORT] [--no-window] [--output DIRECTORY]
```

Watch `.rocdown` sources, `rocdown.toml`, and assets, rebuild, and serve the site
with live reload. The default root is the current directory. Preview output
goes to a temp directory unless `--output` is set. The preview window supports
current-document find and `Cmd/Ctrl-K` jump-to-page using `/pages.json`. The
Dev control opens a profiling panel at `/__rocci/dev`. `rocdown run` and
`rocdown build` refuse OKF knowledge records and bundles and point to
`rocci-okf run`.

| Option | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `--no-window` | Serve without opening the preview window |
| `--port PORT` | Override the listening port |
| `--output DIRECTORY` | Write preview files here instead of a temp directory |

### Build documentation

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- build [ROOT] [--output DIRECTORY]
```

The default root is the current directory. `ROOT` may be a documentation
directory or a `.rocdown` file. `rocdown.toml` is optional. `--output` overrides
`build.output`. OKF knowledge records are refused here as well.

Local `:img` and Markdown image paths resolve against the source file. Missing
local files fail the catalog (`RD2103`). Files under `build.assets` are
content-hashed whether the authored URL is `/assets/foo.png` or `assets/foo.png`.

### Check documentation

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- check [ROOT] [--format terminal|json]
```

Validate the catalog, including article-block content models, includes, page links,
and local assets, without compiling Roc or writing output.

### Test documented examples

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- test [ROOT] [--update] [--format terminal|json]
```

Run `:example` commands that declare `test`. `--update` rewrites golden
files named by `expect`.

### Inspect Rocdown AST and planned artifacts

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- inspect ast FILE.rocdown
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- inspect artifacts [ROOT]
```

---

## Rocci OKF CLI

### Validate knowledge bundle

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- check [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci] [--format terminal|json]
```

Base mode checks OKF v0.2. Rocci mode additionally validates approved types,
tags, lifecycle, provenance, authority, and owner fields.

### Inspect knowledge catalog, concept, and graph

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- inspect concept ID [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- inspect catalog [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- inspect graph [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
```

### Search knowledge records

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- search QUERY [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
```

### Retrieval benchmarks

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- benchmark BENCHMARK_FILE [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
```

Measures top-5 hit rate and mean reciprocal rank against versioned questions and
enforces passing thresholds.

### Live review preview server

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- run [PATH] [--profile base|rocci] [--port PORT] [--no-window]
```

`PATH` may be a bundle directory, a concept Markdown file inside a bundle, or
the bundle-root `index.md`. A concept file opens the review site on that
record. The preview window supports current-document find and `Cmd/Ctrl-K`
jump-to-record using `/catalog.json`. The Dev control opens a profiling panel
at `/__rocci/dev`.

### Build static review artifacts

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- build [ROOT] [--output DIRECTORY] [--profile base|rocci]
```
